# K02c: no caller on the way binds `copy`, so read's hidden input falls back to its lexical source -- the unit-level
# merge result (value 1) -- the last of the three sources (the book §12).  Success is 7.
Model: (int: value 1)
copy: merge: Model
fn: read () int
return: copy\value
fn: plain () int
return: read()
int: result plain()
if: result != 1
    sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 81; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
    return
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: 7; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
